Behold! It is possible to map the keyboard for nethack!

First will kill the statement IBM_BIOS in the cnf file.

after that, the rest is simple: place in a batch file without 'echo off'
all the prompt escape sequences remapping the keyboard. f1-f10 can be remapped,
as well as shft-f1-f10 (but those seem redundant, for the reason for remapping,
was to reduce the number of key strokes).

command: prompt $e[key1;key2p

key1 = key to be changed
key2 = what to change key1 into.
p - simply issues the remapping.

personally I changed Q to q and f10 to Q
furthermore, the tilde key (top left on 101 ext. keyb.) is always the E-word.

frog.

